<title>JAPAN: Fuji Electronics says to buy back 600,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Fuji Electronics says to buy back 600,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Fuji Electronics Co Ltd said on Monday it would spend up to 500 million yen to buy back 600,000 of its shares.</p>
<p>It said the repurchase was subject to approval by a shareholders' meeting on May 22.</p>
<p>Fuji Electronics sells semiconductors, integrated circuits and electronic equipment. As of February 1, it had 11.522 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>The shares closes at 670 yen on Monday.</p>
</text>
